title: Tariff
text: White goods come down the fenced road, and each border takes its cut. But the customs sheds stand off the road, and the goods must be seen there still untaxed. Wherever the road is left, it carries on from that same spot.
trick: a quad bender on the road turns the beam off it on one face; after a loop through the shed, where a filter takes the duty, the beam comes back on the other face and leaves along the road again, as if the piece were not there. A filter on the road itself lights the exit but can never show the untaxed goods
motif: pictogram (a road between two fences with a gate every other square, a customs yard each side)
expect: recolours>=2
proof: not proved; no other solution found in 300 s
